Participants:
- Alex Vance (CEO & Co-Founder, AetherFlow AI)
- Dr. Elena Rostova (CTO & Co-Founder, AetherFlow AI)
- Jordan Hayes (General Partner, Frontline Ventures)
- Context: Board Review of Q3 Traction, Runway Pressure & Headcount Allocation

00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:09.000
Jordan Hayes: Welcome everyone. Let's jump straight to the numbers. Alex, you sent over the August financial model. Cash balance is at $740K, burning around $74K net per month.

00:00:09.500 --> 00:00:19.000
Alex Vance: Thanks Jordan. Yes, our MRR reached $82K this month, representing 14% month-over-month growth. However, our cash out date sits at late May 2027—leaving us approximately 9 months of runway.

00:00:19.500 --> 00:00:29.000
Jordan Hayes: 9 months is the danger zone for a Seed-stage company. You need to start your Series A process in January when you still have 5 months of buffer. You cannot afford any uncontrolled burn expansion.

00:00:29.500 --> 00:00:41.000
Dr. Elena Rostova: Jordan, on the engineering side, Liam and I are feeling heavy pressure on infrastructure. We want to open a requisition for a Senior Infrastructure Engineer at $14,000 per month ($168K annualized).

00:00:41.500 --> 00:00:53.000
Jordan Hayes: Elena, if you add $14K a month in fixed payroll right now, your net burn spikes from $74K to $88K. That pulls your zero-cash date forward by a full 6 weeks into April 2027.

00:00:53.500 --> 00:01:05.000
Alex Vance: That's the tension. However, Sarah is negotiating an $80K ARR pilot with Acme Corp. If Sarah closes Acme, that adds $6,667 in monthly revenue, which offsets nearly half of that infrastructure engineer's salary.

00:01:05.500 --> 00:01:17.000
Jordan Hayes: Here is my board guidance: Do not extend an offer to that infrastructure engineer until the Acme Corp contract is signed and cash is in the bank. Keep your fixed burn locked down.

00:01:17.500 --> 00:01:28.000
Alex Vance: Understood, Jordan. We will hold the hiring requisition until Acme Corp signs the MSA. We stay disciplined, protect our 9 months of runway, and prioritize revenue-backed hiring.